1
00:04:18,057 --> 00:04:48,037
We'll be right back.

2
00:04:48,057 --> 00:05:18,037
We'll be right back.

3
00:05:18,057 --> 00:05:48,037
We'll be right back.

4
00:05:48,057 --> 00:05:51,857
The steam whistle forces friends apart.

5
00:05:52,237 --> 00:05:53,897
The C-Train starts to run.

6
00:05:56,057 --> 00:05:58,557
All right, I'll give you one last chance.

7
00:05:58,797 --> 00:06:03,737
I'll call off my mid-fernell, but once we're on that train, they're gonna tear you limb from limb.

8
00:06:03,997 --> 00:06:04,877
Listen, jerks.

9
00:06:04,877 --> 00:06:06,877
If I were you, I'd quit while I was in...

10
00:06:06,877 --> 00:06:07,697
Oh, come on.

11
00:06:08,637 --> 00:06:09,837
Why is he here?

12
00:06:13,917 --> 00:06:16,457
Excellent work as always, sirs and madam.

13
00:06:16,457 --> 00:06:20,897
Here, Mr. Lutia, Colt.

14
00:06:21,257 --> 00:06:22,617
What is this, a parade?

15
00:06:23,677 --> 00:06:24,397
Stop it.

16
00:06:24,577 --> 00:06:25,217
It's foolish.

17
00:06:25,417 --> 00:06:26,397
Ah, right.

18
00:06:26,657 --> 00:06:27,317
Sorry, sir.

19
00:06:27,317 --> 00:06:33,597
This isn't over until we reach Eni's lobby, so look sharp.

20
00:06:33,857 --> 00:06:35,957
Everyone board the C-Train immediately.

21
00:06:36,757 --> 00:06:37,757
You heard the man.

22
00:06:38,077 --> 00:06:39,877
Get on the train and make it quick.

23
00:06:39,877 --> 00:06:43,677
Hey, you bastard's gonna put me down or...

24
00:06:43,677 --> 00:06:48,497
Who are those guys in the suits?

25
00:06:48,497 --> 00:06:57,097
He says he's sorry for causing us so much trouble.

26
00:06:57,417 --> 00:06:59,917
Then he goes and gets in trouble all over again.

27
00:07:00,957 --> 00:07:02,637
A little further to the right!

28
00:07:02,937 --> 00:07:04,017
Spray over there!

29
00:07:04,157 --> 00:07:05,477
Bring the hose this way!

30
00:07:06,757 --> 00:07:07,957
We've almost got it!

31
00:07:07,977 --> 00:07:09,437
I think we're good over here for now.

32
00:07:09,617 --> 00:07:11,137
Go see if you can help out with the injure.

33
00:07:11,397 --> 00:07:11,757
Right!

34
00:07:11,977 --> 00:07:12,617
I'm on it!

35
00:07:12,937 --> 00:07:14,357
Is there anyone left inside?

36
00:07:14,537 --> 00:07:14,877
Hey!

37
00:07:15,057 --> 00:07:16,297
Watch your step over there!

38
00:07:16,577 --> 00:07:18,437
So, you mean Robin?

39
00:07:18,497 --> 00:07:20,357
Robin doesn't hate us after all?

40
00:07:20,677 --> 00:07:21,217
Uh-huh!

41
00:07:21,997 --> 00:07:23,157
I'm so happy!

42
00:07:23,757 --> 00:07:24,017
Huh?

43
00:07:24,217 --> 00:07:25,257
He's a raccoon dog?

44
00:07:25,277 --> 00:07:26,517
I thought he was a reindeer.

45
00:07:27,117 --> 00:07:29,157
Did he just transform or what?

46
00:07:29,397 --> 00:07:33,837
Anyway, Chopper, we have to find the rest of the crew right away so we can go rescue Robin.

47
00:07:34,057 --> 00:07:35,577
Okay, let's go!

48
00:07:35,857 --> 00:07:37,997
Uh, but where are they?

49
00:07:38,377 --> 00:07:38,997
I don't know.

50
00:07:39,177 --> 00:07:40,437
That's why we have to find them.

51
00:07:41,657 --> 00:07:42,137
Yeah!

52
00:07:42,477 --> 00:07:43,857
Let's do this!

53
00:07:44,017 --> 00:07:44,297
Whoa!

54
00:07:45,097 --> 00:07:46,217
Now he's a gorilla!

55
00:07:46,217 --> 00:07:48,877
Wait, you two.

56
00:07:49,637 --> 00:07:49,837
Huh?

57
00:07:51,937 --> 00:08:00,317
I don't care if you go after Nico Robin, but before you run off, you should know that the C-Train for government personnel is departing at 11 o'clock tonight.

58
00:08:00,317 --> 00:08:04,977
This is just my guess, but there's a good chance you'll find CP-9 there.

59
00:08:05,417 --> 00:08:08,657
And that means Nico Robin will be there as well.

60
00:08:09,457 --> 00:08:13,317
Thanks to Aqua Laguna, they're stopping all service after this final departure.

61
00:08:13,957 --> 00:08:17,437
In other words, you won't be able to chase him on another train.

62
00:08:17,437 --> 00:08:20,137
Wait, you mean we have to...

63
00:08:20,137 --> 00:08:20,557
Hmm.

64
00:08:21,197 --> 00:08:26,837
Since you obviously can't sail in this weather, you won't be able to leave the island unless you go after that train right now.

65
00:08:27,077 --> 00:08:27,437
Huh?

66
00:08:27,597 --> 00:08:28,397
No way!

67
00:08:28,577 --> 00:08:29,617
What time is it?

68
00:08:29,657 --> 00:08:30,537
Almost 10.30.

69
00:08:30,657 --> 00:08:30,977
What?

70
00:08:31,117 --> 00:08:33,137
That means we've only got half an hour left!

71
00:08:33,557 --> 00:08:35,277
Hey, but you're the mayor, right?

72
00:08:35,357 --> 00:08:37,137
Can't you do something to stop the train?

73
00:08:37,137 --> 00:08:43,197
Well, unfortunately, it's bound for Eni's lobby, which is only accessible to government personnel.

74
00:08:43,637 --> 00:08:47,557
Even the engine driver works for the government, so I have no say in this matter.

75
00:08:47,717 --> 00:08:48,277
Oh, no.

76
00:08:49,137 --> 00:08:53,877
I guess our only choice is to head to the station and try to talk some sense into Robin.

77
00:08:54,417 --> 00:08:54,817
Chopper?

78
00:08:55,017 --> 00:08:55,197
Huh?

79
00:08:55,937 --> 00:08:59,977
I'll tell you which direction Luffy and Zoro flew off in, so you go search there, okay?

80
00:09:00,417 --> 00:09:03,257
If you find them, tell them to come to the station as quickly as they can.

81
00:09:03,377 --> 00:09:04,417
Okay, got it!

82
00:09:04,417 --> 00:09:07,497
Hey, listen up!

83
00:09:07,997 --> 00:09:09,117
Oh, look, you guys!

84
00:09:09,297 --> 00:09:09,937
Polly's okay!

85
00:09:10,637 --> 00:09:12,097
See that girl over there?

86
00:09:12,577 --> 00:09:14,477
I want you to help her find her buddies.

87
00:09:15,877 --> 00:09:18,237
You sure that smoke didn't get in your brain, Polly?

88
00:09:18,437 --> 00:09:20,637
These are the guys that tried to kill Mr. Iceberg!

89
00:09:20,777 --> 00:09:22,637
We should ring their no-good sorry necks!

90
00:09:23,057 --> 00:09:27,917
Besides, why should we waste our time helping some criminals when Luchi and Kaku are still missing?

91
00:09:27,957 --> 00:09:30,077
The Straw Hats aren't the ones who did it, okay?

92
00:09:30,357 --> 00:09:32,117
The real criminals set them up!

93
00:09:32,497 --> 00:09:34,097
We hadn't been so damn blind.

94
00:09:34,097 --> 00:09:36,337
We wouldn't be in this situation right now.

95
00:09:36,897 --> 00:09:43,057
I don't know the real identity of those guys in the masks, but I do know that the Straw Hats tried to protect us from them.

96
00:09:43,457 --> 00:09:49,037
As a matter of fact, Iceberg and I wouldn't even be alive right now if it wasn't for their help.

97
00:09:49,037 --> 00:09:54,377
Don't bother looking for Luchi and Kaku.

98
00:09:54,997 --> 00:09:56,157
There's no point.

99
00:09:56,637 --> 00:09:59,437
In fact, I don't know if we'll ever be seeing them again.

100
00:09:59,437 --> 00:10:03,277
What? If you know what happened to the foreman, then you gotta tell us, Polly.

101
00:10:04,237 --> 00:10:05,737
They went back home.

102
00:10:05,837 --> 00:10:08,397
Huh? Why would they do that at a time like this?

103
00:10:08,397 --> 00:10:10,397
Just shut up and go find Straw Hat.

104
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:12,137
Hey, immoral girl.

105
00:10:12,677 --> 00:10:14,797
What? You're still calling me that?

106
00:10:14,797 --> 00:10:17,437
If you're going to the station, I'll show you the way.

107
00:10:17,677 --> 00:10:19,417
Uh, thanks, I guess.

108
00:10:20,137 --> 00:10:23,757
Hey, hold on a sec, Polly. Is that stuff you told us true?

109
00:10:24,317 --> 00:10:28,517
Quit your yapping and help them out already! You're making Galilaw look bad!

110
00:10:28,517 --> 00:10:30,517
Yes! Sorry, sir!

111
00:10:30,717 --> 00:10:31,717
We'll do our best!

112
00:10:31,777 --> 00:10:32,597
You're the boss!

113
00:10:32,637 --> 00:10:34,517
Yeah! We'll help any way we can!

114
00:10:34,977 --> 00:10:37,157
Open the cage! Bring out the Yagadas!

115
00:10:37,437 --> 00:10:37,797
Yeah!

116
00:10:40,257 --> 00:10:42,077
Went back home, did they?

117
00:10:44,297 --> 00:10:47,677
I spared them the details. It's better that way.

118
00:10:48,037 --> 00:10:52,957
It was bad enough when we found out they deserved the truth, but I don't want to hurt those guys.

119
00:10:58,517 --> 00:11:15,297
Hey, Chopper, it's all up to you now!

120
00:11:16,617 --> 00:11:20,517
Right! All my Lupian Zorro, you can count on me!

121
00:11:20,517 --> 00:11:50,497
You can count on me!

122
00:11:50,497 --> 00:11:51,897
Hey, guys, can you hear me?

123
00:11:52,297 --> 00:11:52,857
Luffy!

124
00:11:54,177 --> 00:11:54,737
Zorro!

125
00:11:55,457 --> 00:11:56,137
Sanji!

126
00:11:57,577 --> 00:11:59,817
Usap, you can come with us too, okay?

127
00:12:00,517 --> 00:12:02,217
Now shed it with me!

128
00:12:02,377 --> 00:12:05,377
All right, buddy, you got it! Let's do it, guys!

129
00:12:06,737 --> 00:12:08,517
Hey! Luffy!

130
00:12:09,437 --> 00:12:10,157
Zorro!

131
00:12:11,277 --> 00:12:11,917
Sanji!

132
00:12:13,417 --> 00:12:15,477
Usap, you can come with us too!

133
00:12:20,497 --> 00:12:25,857
Take that canal over on the left-hand side! It's a shortcut to the station!

134
00:12:25,857 --> 00:12:38,597
We still have 20 minutes before the train leaves.

135
00:12:39,377 --> 00:12:40,597
Don't go, Robin.

136
00:12:41,037 --> 00:12:43,177
You don't have to sacrifice yourself.

137
00:12:43,777 --> 00:12:45,077
We can save you!

138
00:12:45,777 --> 00:12:49,017
Mr. Yagada, you think you can go a little bit faster, please?

139
00:12:49,017 --> 00:12:50,237
Move, move, move!

140
00:13:00,237 --> 00:13:03,137
The 11 o'clock train is about to depart.

141
00:13:03,597 --> 00:13:06,977
All passengers going from Blue Station to Emmy's Lobby.

142
00:13:07,337 --> 00:13:08,637
Please board immediately.

143
00:13:11,297 --> 00:13:13,317
That hurts!

144
00:13:13,317 --> 00:13:15,397
I don't want to hear another word out of you two.

145
00:13:15,517 --> 00:13:18,657
Well, maybe I wouldn't complain so much if you weren't such big jerkwads!

146
00:13:18,677 --> 00:13:20,037
Yeah, you big jerkwads!

147
00:13:20,097 --> 00:13:21,697
Why don't you come over here and fight?

148
00:13:21,857 --> 00:13:23,277
Hey, that's too much!

149
00:13:27,457 --> 00:13:29,697
Due to the approaching storm surge,

150
00:13:29,997 --> 00:13:31,797
the departure time has been moved up

151
00:13:31,797 --> 00:13:33,457
and the train will be departing shortly.

152
00:13:33,877 --> 00:13:34,397
Damn it.

153
00:13:34,657 --> 00:13:36,217
This was bad enough already.

154
00:13:36,217 --> 00:13:42,137
After all these years,

155
00:13:42,237 --> 00:13:44,157
our mission has finally come to an end.

156
00:13:44,297 --> 00:13:45,417
We're not there yet.

157
00:13:45,697 --> 00:13:46,777
Stop spouting nonsense

158
00:13:46,777 --> 00:13:49,077
and take your mission seriously, you fool.

159
00:13:49,997 --> 00:13:50,977
My apologies.

160
00:13:54,857 --> 00:13:56,537
You can't sail in this weather.

161
00:13:56,917 --> 00:13:58,477
Unless you can catch that train,

162
00:13:58,837 --> 00:14:00,077
you won't be able to leave.

163
00:14:00,277 --> 00:14:01,017
Come on!

164
00:14:01,237 --> 00:14:02,417
We're so close!

165
00:14:02,417 --> 00:14:02,977
Woo!

166
00:14:03,597 --> 00:14:03,917
Woo!

167
00:14:06,217 --> 00:14:13,857
Frankie,

168
00:14:14,457 --> 00:14:16,037
wherever you are,

169
00:14:16,277 --> 00:14:17,617
I hope you're safe.

170
00:14:27,777 --> 00:14:29,717
Hey, Lupe!

171
00:14:30,657 --> 00:14:32,197
Row, row, go away!

172
00:14:32,397 --> 00:14:32,837
Lupe!

173
00:14:33,597 --> 00:14:34,117
Hey!

174
00:14:34,697 --> 00:14:35,677
Come back!

175
00:14:36,217 --> 00:14:38,217
Who are you?

176
00:14:38,217 --> 00:14:40,217
Come on, there's not much time!

177
00:14:40,217 --> 00:14:44,217
Zoro! Sanji!

178
00:14:44,217 --> 00:14:47,217
Musa, you can come too.

179
00:14:47,217 --> 00:14:52,217
Luffy! Please, those guys are gonna take Robin away!

180
00:14:52,217 --> 00:14:55,217
We need your help! Where are you?

181
00:14:55,217 --> 00:15:08,217
I wonder how the rest of the crew is dealing with this mess.

182
00:15:08,217 --> 00:15:12,217
Anyway, time's up. They'll have to catch me later.

183
00:15:12,217 --> 00:15:16,217
I repeat, the final train will be departing ahead of schedule.

184
00:15:16,217 --> 00:15:18,217
Please board immediately.

185
00:15:25,217 --> 00:15:27,217
You bastards!

186
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:31,217
I'm coming for you! Just wait, you'll see!

187
00:15:35,217 --> 00:15:37,217
Once I get out of here!

188
00:15:37,217 --> 00:15:41,217
My little slip-up, then this crap happens!

189
00:15:45,217 --> 00:15:47,217
I'm coming for you bastards!

190
00:15:49,217 --> 00:15:51,217
Once I get out of here!

191
00:15:55,217 --> 00:16:00,217
Help me! Zoro! Sanji!

192
00:16:00,217 --> 00:16:02,217
Where are you?

193
00:16:03,217 --> 00:16:05,217
We gotta save Robin!

194
00:16:05,217 --> 00:16:06,217
Zoro!

195
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:09,217
Roronewa!

196
00:16:15,217 --> 00:16:17,217
I don't get it. Where in the heck are they?

197
00:16:17,217 --> 00:16:19,217
Have we checked over there yet?

198
00:16:19,217 --> 00:16:20,217
Hey!

199
00:16:20,217 --> 00:16:21,217
Roronewa!

200
00:16:21,217 --> 00:16:22,217
Zoro!

201
00:16:22,217 --> 00:16:24,217
I guess they're not here.

202
00:16:24,217 --> 00:16:26,217
Has anybody checked over in the back streets yet?

203
00:16:26,217 --> 00:16:28,217
I don't know if we can.

204
00:16:28,217 --> 00:16:30,217
They're probably completely flooded by now.

205
00:16:30,217 --> 00:16:32,217
It'd be too dangerous to look for them there.

206
00:16:32,217 --> 00:16:34,217
Come on, guys!

207
00:16:34,217 --> 00:16:35,217
Where are you?

208
00:16:35,217 --> 00:16:37,217
There's no time!

209
00:16:37,217 --> 00:16:38,217
Time!

210
00:16:50,217 --> 00:16:51,217
Excuse me!

211
00:16:51,217 --> 00:16:56,217
The waves are getting dangerously high, so we've decided to depart early as a safety measure.

212
00:16:56,217 --> 00:16:57,217
If there's any trouble, we could...

213
00:16:57,217 --> 00:16:58,217
It's fine. Just go.

214
00:16:58,217 --> 00:16:59,217
Just go.

215
00:16:59,217 --> 00:17:00,217
Just go.

216
00:17:00,217 --> 00:17:01,217
Just go.

217
00:17:01,217 --> 00:17:03,217
Just go.

218
00:21:55,180 --> 00:22:12,180
夢見た僕らは間違いじゃないと信じて 荒く埋める海原を渡って行ける

219
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:22,180
誰よりも勇敢で思いやりもあるけれど

220
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:32,180
もしも君がこの船を降りて 違う世界にいたとしても

221
00:22:32,180 --> 00:22:40,180
最後にはきっと笑えるよ

222
00:22:52,180 --> 00:23:01,180
誰かを サンジー乗ろう人と思ったら

223
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:08,180
どうも 大丈夫を変 θにする

224
00:23:08,180 --> 00:23:09,880
Sanji barges in!

225
00:23:09,880 --> 00:23:11,880
C-Train battle in the storm!

226
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:13,880
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

